GPUI's Windows backend compiles its HLSL shaders with fxc.exe behind
`#[cfg(target_os = "windows")]`, which in a build script means the *host*.
Cross-compiled from Linux, the script therefore does nothing, and the release
build fails on the missing `shaders_bytes.rs`. (A debug build compiles the
shaders at run time from a source path on the build machine, so it is not
something to ship either.)

This asks about the *target* instead, and on a non-Windows host runs fxc.exe
through wine, or whatever GPUI_FXC_RUNNER names. Only build.rs changes.

build-aux/build-windows.sh applies it to the copy of the crate cargo has
unpacked. Drop it when the pinned GPUI no longer needs it; it is tied to
0.3.7 by name so that a version bump fails loudly instead of silently
building without it.

